  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Women-Owned Small Business (WOSB) set-aside contracts totaled $629M in FY2026 to date. Award activity reached 2,087 obligations, with an average award size of $301K, and obligations fell 50.3% year over year. Fiscal-year listings show a decline from earlier peaks: FY21 totaled $856M, FY22 totaled $934M, FY23 totaled $1.2B, FY24 totaled $1.3B, and FY25 totaled $1.3B. The Department of Defense obligated $308M in FY2026 to date, followed by the Department of Homeland Security with $81.9M and the Department of Commerce with $55.3M. Other leading agencies include the Department of Health and Human Services with $43.7M and the Department of Justice with $24.1M. Top vendors in the period include INTELLECT SOLUTIONS, LLC with $18.5M and DTECHLOGIC LLC with $17.4M. Leading industries are Other Computer Related Services with $112M and Engineering Services with $111M. These figures are contract obligations and represent fiscal year to date totals, not full-year results.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Why did obligations fall year over year?",
        "body": "Fiscal-year obligations for WOSB set-asides are down 50.3% in FY2026 to date. The current total is $629M compared with prior-year totals that ranged from $856M to $1.3B. Agency-level concentration is high: the Department of Defense accounted for $308M of the FY2026 total. Those two facts together show a smaller FY2026-to-date spend that remains concentrated in a few big buyers."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies, vendors, and industries dominate FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer with $308M in obligations, followed by the Department of Homeland Security with $81.9M and the Department of Commerce with $55.3M. INTELLECT SOLUTIONS, LLC leads vendors with $18.5M, followed by DTECHLOGIC LLC with $17.4M and FCN, INC. with $16.4M. Other Computer Related Services and Engineering Services are the largest industries with $112M and $111M in obligations respectively."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does the federal government award through WOSB set-asides?",
      "a": "The federal government awarded $629M through WOSB set-asides in FY2026 to date. Those obligations came in 2,087 awards with an average award size of $301K, and obligations are down 50.3% year over year. Fiscal-year history shows higher totals in prior years, including $1.3B in both FY24 and FY25."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies use WOSB set-asides the most?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense uses WOSB set-asides the most, with $308M in obligations in FY2026 to date. The Department of Homeland Security follows with $81.9M and the Department of Commerce follows with $55.3M. Other notable buyers include the Department of Health and Human Services with $43.7M and the Department of Justice with $24.1M."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are the largest WOSB set-aside contractors?",
